<title>USA: TNP says competition plan approved.</title>
<headline>TNP says competition plan approved.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texas-New Mexico Power Co said Thursday the New Mexico Public Utility Commission approved the company's plan for allowing its New Mexico customers to choose their energy provider.</p>
<p>According to the plan, the company's customers in New Mexico, starting Tuesday, will will begin a three-year transition period, at the end of which they will have a choice of energy suppliers at market rates, the company said.</p>
<p>This marks the first time the state's energy customers will have a choice in energy supply.</p>
</text>
